## What to build

One Google Colab notebook. Keep it minimal — I want to read and understand every line.

**Part 1 — Parse.** Turn all 8,945 lines into a pandas DataFrame, one row per attempt,
one column per field. Turn the leading timestamp into a real datetime, not text.
Print the number of rows and the column names so I can see it worked.

**Part 2 — Signal 1: brute force.** One source trying password after password.
Find every source IP address where the number of FAILED attempts inside any rolling
60-second window is MORE THAN 5. "Rolling" means slide a 60-second window along the
timeline — not fixed clock minutes. "More than 5" means 6 or more.
Print a small table: IP address, total failures, most failures in any 60-second window,
and the country.

**Part 3 — Signal 2: distributed attack.** The opposite shape — one account attacked
from many places at once. Find the account (use the uid field) with the most failed
attempts, then report: how many attempts against it in total, how many of those failed,
how many distinct source IPs were used, and how many distinct countries.

**Part 4 — Summary.** Print a short plain-English summary of what the tool found.

